            <ArticleTitle>Fabry disease and Factor V Leiden: a potent vascular risk combination.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>422-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1445-5994.2011.02483.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 45-year-old man with heterozygous Factor V Leiden presented with his third cerebrovascular accident despite being on warfarin at a therapeutic international normalized ratio. Subsequent investigation revealed a second genetic diagnosis of Fabry disease. He then had an acute myocardial infarction whilst on aspirin and warfarin.</AbstractText>
